\
# Technology Selection Rationale\
\
## Java\
\
Java was selected because it provides strong object-oriented programming support and integrates well with enterprise frameworks.\
\
## Spring Boot\
\
Spring Boot simplifies REST API development and dependency management while supporting modular application design.\
\
## PostgreSQL\
\
PostgreSQL offers reliability, ACID compliance, and excellent support for transactional systems.\
\
## RabbitMQ\
\
RabbitMQ enables asynchronous event processing and reduces coupling between modules.\
\
## Maven\
\
Maven provides standardized project management and dependency handling.\
\
## Mermaid\
\
Mermaid enables version-controlled diagrams that integrate well with GitHub.\
\
## JMeter\
\
JMeter will be used to validate the Reservation API under heavy concurrent load.\
\
## Postman\
\
Postman provides a simple way to test and document REST endpoints.\
\
---\
\
# Conclusion\
\
The selected technology stack provides a maintainable, scalable, and enterprise-oriented foundation for the BitePlate Smart Restaurant Management System.}